{"id": "EV-R-adoption-tests", "version": 2, "type": "evidence", "tier": "candidate", "evidence_kind": "contract_conformance", "text": "tests/test_adoption_friction.py: 30 tests, each group written first and failing before its change (19 of 22, then 7 of 8): no-code repo, --hooks/--no-hooks, purpose text and a verified purpose anchor, refusal with nothing written, --ci-name default/custom/invalid, aec anchor (checked, rationale, unresolved, outside the repo), and aec append (computed and alias-root anchors, prefix_bytes, duplicate and check-rejected records refused byte-for-byte, dry run, stdin, missing final newline). Full suite 300 passed, 1 skipped", "relations": [{"rel": "supports", "to": "CL-R-adoption@2"}, {"rel": "supersedes", "to": "EV-R-adoption-tests@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-P0", "version": 3, "type": "purpose", "subject": "aec-purpose", "epistemic": "committed", "owner": "AU-zach", "text": "Telosmith helps people and AI agents build, understand, govern, and evolve tools while preserving why those tools exist and what they must accomplish. It connects executable implementations with living semantic records of purpose, requirements, rationale, decisions, evidence, and uncertainty; makes consequential changes visible for reconsideration; and supports legitimate restructuring without silently discarding commitments. It operates alongside Spec Kit, within other agentic coding systems, or independently. Its structural findings inform human judgment rather than replace it, and its value must be demonstrated against simpler approaches, accounting for the cost of maintaining its records.", "quote": "Accepted", "origin": "Zach, Cockpit Choices, 2026-11-05 14:16 CT (recorded by the coordinator, session 01GZK2KncnZ4v7e6ZAQ4C1ZH)", "rationale": "Owner adoption of the purpose text Kate drafted (Telosmith as tool builder), recorded in the owner's private decision log as DEC-116 (superseding DEC-094); step 1 of Kate's two-week plan, which the owner accepted on 2026-11-05 at 14:38 CT (DEC-121). The text is Kate's draft verbatim. It keeps P0@2's three capacities (alongside Spec Kit, within other agentic coding systems, independently) and adds that findings inform human judgment and that value must be shown against simpler approaches net of record cost. Dual-Channel Coding is not part of it (deferred, DEC-121).", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-P0@2"}], "anchors": [{"path": "governance/decisions.jsonl", "sha256": "9bb6fb028aa5f3bf03c43c31a8640f0a522fb2a5a616c478772183f98ef313a5", "locator": "q:\"id\": \"DEC-116\"", "for": "rationale", "root": "relay-kit-private", "prefix_bytes": 123944}]}
{"id": "AEC-R3", "version": 3, "type": "requirement", "subject": "aec-purpose", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "Adoption is earned against a well-configured baseline for the setup in use, with authoring cost counted; if equal, simplify Telosmith. Spec Kit is one supported setup, where the baseline is a well-configured Spec Kit; in another agentic coding system the baseline is that system well configured without Telosmith, and standalone it is the same work without Telosmith", "rationale": "Follows from AEC-P0@2: with three capacities Spec Kit can no longer be the only baseline. Only the baseline clause changed; authoring cost and 'if equal, simplify' are kept. The non-Spec-Kit baseline wording is the lane builder's reading of DEC-079 ('AEC-R3 no longer makes Spec Kit the baseline'), not Zach's words; he may reword it. @3: re-pinned from AEC-P0@2 to AEC-P0@3 (the owner's adoption of Kate's purpose text, DEC-116); text unchanged; P0@3 keeps the three capacities this requirement serves.", "quote": "Amend Telosmith's purpose to include Spec Kit Compatibility, Extension of other Agentic Coding Systems, and a Standalone capacity.", "origin": "Zach, Claude cowork session 01GZK2KncnZ4v7e6ZAQ4C1ZH, 2026-11-04 20:02 CT", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R3@2"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@3"}], "anchors": [{"root": "relay-kit-private", "path": "governance/decisions.jsonl", "sha256": "95fc51d31dbef5ce1cc09347771a0abccafde2ce9783a1da4571192fe11a8444", "locator": "q:\"id\": \"DEC-079\"", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-adoption", "version": 3, "type": "requirement", "subject": "aec-scope", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Adopting Telosmith in another repository needs no hand-hashing and no hand-editing of the purpose stub: init takes the purpose (and a cited passage) directly, writes the hook and CI only where there is Python code, and names the CI workflow as asked (default aec); aec anchor prints a checked anchor and aec append adds a record with computed anchors, refusing duplicates and records check would reject. Adopters cite outside decisions (a private ledger) as text only. Scope from handoff HO-AEC-20261105-PPPP", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-adoption@2"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@3"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:src.aec.init.init"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:src.aec.append.build"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:src.aec.append.make_anchor"}], "anchors": [{"path": "governance/decisions.jsonl", "sha256": "5624a3ccb4519e9a79511f91f655458d7066940b8614520ab6a859d437e7046d", "locator": "q:\"id\": \"DEC-095\"", "for": "rationale", "root": "relay-kit-private", "prefix_bytes": 94205}], "rationale": "@3: re-pinned from AEC-P0@2 to AEC-P0@3 (the owner's adoption of Kate's purpose text, DEC-116); text unchanged; P0@3 keeps the three capacities this requirement serves."}
