{"id": "AEC-R-hook-line-unavailable", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Requirement: When the launcher cannot import `aec`, or imports an `aec` that lacks `hook project`, it shall emit a diagnostic distinguishing those conditions and exit 1.", "test_must_show": ["Isolated missing-package and older-package fixtures produce distinguishable diagnostics and exit 1.", "Neither condition is silently treated as success or falls back to the inline body."], "out_of_scope": "automatic installation, upgrades, and CI-pin comparison.", "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5--0506d49d889c.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-18T01:22:18Z). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261118-03: requirement into text, her 'Test must show' and 'Out of scope' bullets into test_must_show and out_of_scope; relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private 16dc713, handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5.md (the round-2 ask and the wake summary only); not the PR diff, the tests or the text of AEC-R-hook-line@1. Implementation conformance: not assessed by the maintainer.", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-hook-line-pin-gate", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Requirement: No existing repository hook shall be replaced with the line hook until that launcher enforces a check that its locally resolved `aec` version equals the repository’s CI pin, refusing execution with a diagnostic and exit 1 when equality cannot be established.", "test_must_show": ["Matching versions permit execution.", "Mismatch, missing or unreadable pin, and indeterminate local version prevent body execution.", "A blocked replacement leaves existing settings unchanged."], "out_of_scope": "selecting the shared pin-file format, installing the pinned release, and authorizing rollout.", "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5--0506d49d889c.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-18T01:22:18Z). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261118-03: requirement into text, her 'Test must show' and 'Out of scope' bullets into test_must_show and out_of_scope; relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private 16dc713, handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5.md (the round-2 ask and the wake summary only); not the PR diff, the tests or the text of AEC-R-hook-line@1. Implementation conformance: not assessed by the maintainer.", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-hook-project-parity", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Requirement: Given equivalent checkout state, inline and line hooks shall preserve the same outcome contract—0 without a report, 1 when a required step cannot run, and 2 with an agent report—and shall refuse symlinks at `.aec`, the records file, or either output without writing through them.", "test_must_show": ["Run each hook against independently restored copies of each fixture, covering all three outcomes and report presence.", "Exercise each prohibited symlink separately, including dangling links.", "Verify both hooks exit 2, report the symlink refusal, and neither modify nor create the symlink target."], "out_of_scope": "byte-identical report formatting and filesystem race-resistance beyond these path checks.", "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5--95f315f3cde3.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-18T03:17:54Z): she ruled exit 2 satisfies the requirement, called 'verify exit 1' an over-specific test expectation, and gave the replacement line, to be appended as a new version preserving @1. Transcribed by claude:aec#wake-20261118-05: text, out_of_scope and test line 1 unchanged from @1; @1's line 2 split at its semicolon, its first clause kept verbatim, its second clause replaced by her replacement sentence verbatim.", "shown": "relay-kit-private, handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5.md round-3 ask (the exit-code question and the full text of AEC-R-hook-line@1); not the PR diff, the tests or her four record payloads. Implementation conformance: not assessed by the maintainer.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-hook-project-parity@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-hook-line", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "aec init --hook-style line writes a project hook whose settings text holds only the launcher (the same PYTHONPATH filter and start from / as the inline hook) and calls aec hook project, the hook body shipped in the package. On the same checkout it exits as the inline hook does: 0 when quiet, 1 when a step could not run, 2 with a report for the agent; a symlink at .aec, the records file or either output is refused (exit 2, with a report), without writing through the link or creating its target. When no aec is importable, or the importable aec has no hook project, it says which and exits 1. inline stays the default until the line resolves the version CI pins (Kate gate on Telosmith#88). Out of scope: verifying the installed files (that is the user-level hook) and replacing any repository existing hook.", "source": "Kate round 3 on Telosmith#89 (kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5--95f315f3cde3.md): 'refused' left no writes through links implicit; she found no other contradiction with her records as summarized. Implementer-written.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-hook-line@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:src.aec.userhook.project_run"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-hook-safe-path@6"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/init.py", "sha256": "ed85a5ab20bddc35db46488ebf4c5e2e35fbcd11da5c0e1c7ccea25e6917407e", "locator": "q:HOOK_LINE_COMMAND =", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-pin-check", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "aec pin-check [ROOT] exits 0 only when the local aec equals the Telosmith version the repository's CI pins, and 1 with a one-line reason otherwise. Pins are read from the places repositories already use (each .github/workflows/*.yml|*.yaml line installing git+https://github.com/eraevous/Telosmith.git@<ref>, and tools/aec_upstream.json commit); all pins found must name the same ref. The local version is the commit from PEP 610 direct_url.json, or the HEAD of a clean Telosmith source checkout; anything else is indeterminate and fails. A commit pin matches by prefix; a tag pin matches only an install whose requested revision is that tag (offline, no tag resolution). This is the equality check that Kate's AEC-R-hook-line-pin-gate@1 (on Telosmith#89, not yet on main) asks the one-line hook to enforce. Out of scope: wiring it into the line launcher, defining a new pin-file format, installing the pinned release.", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/pin.py", "sha256": "fa82e593d35b20968a3027dfc5c054964ed5babb650493bfa2705128f0c8b86c", "locator": "q:`aec pin-check`: does the aec running here equal", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-pin-check", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "aec pin-check [ROOT] exits 0 only when the local aec equals the Telosmith version the repository's CI pins, and 1 with a one-line reason otherwise. Pins are read from the places repositories already use (each .github/workflows/*.yml|*.yaml line installing git+https://github.com/eraevous/Telosmith.git@<ref>, and tools/aec_upstream.json commit); all pins found must name the same ref. The local version is the commit from PEP 610 direct_url.json, or the HEAD of a clean Telosmith source checkout; anything else is indeterminate and fails, including a checkout with untracked files in the package (they can shadow committed modules). A commit pin matches by prefix; a release-tag pin (vX.Y[.Z]) matches only an install whose requested revision is that tag (offline, no tag resolution); any other ref, such as main or a branch, is mutable and always fails. This is the equality check that Kate's AEC-R-hook-line-pin-gate@1 (on Telosmith#89, not yet on main) asks the one-line hook to enforce. Out of scope: wiring it into the line launcher, defining a new pin-file format, installing the pinned release.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/pin.py", "sha256": "8a1e0cbdadac62e4b0b30d1013bd35c3fe50a3eeb173e9fc94abab54a42c98b0", "locator": "q:`aec pin-check`: does the aec running here equal", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-pin-check-consensus", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Requirement: `aec pin-check` shall require at least one supported repository pin, require every discovered supported pin to identify the same full 40-character commit, and otherwise exit 1 with a diagnostic.", "test_must_show": ["Matching workflow and JSON pins pass pin validation.", "Missing, malformed, conflicting, abbreviated, tag and `main` pins fail.", "A conflicting second pin cannot be silently ignored."], "out_of_scope": "Other pin formats, remote resolution and changing pins.", "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5--03c3b736dc5d.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-18T13:18:46Z). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261118-15: requirement into text, her 'Test must show' and 'Out of scope' bullets into test_must_show and out_of_scope; markdown bold dropped; relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private 81156ec, handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5.md (the round-4 ask and the wake summary only); not the PR diff, the tests or the text of AEC-R-pin-check@2. Implementation conformance: not assessed by the maintainer.", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-pin-check-local-identity", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Requirement: `aec pin-check` shall exit 0 only when the executing aec’s PEP 610 VCS commit identity, or its clean Telosmith source-checkout HEAD, equals the agreed repository commit; missing, ambiguous or mismatching identity shall exit 1 with a reason.", "test_must_show": ["Exact commit equality succeeds through each supported identity source.", "Different commits, unavailable metadata and unrelated checkouts fail.", "A matching requested tag with a different or unavailable commit fails.", "Identity is taken from the executing installation, not an unrelated checkout."], "out_of_scope": "Verifying installed file contents, signatures or package provenance authenticity.", "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5--03c3b736dc5d.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-18T13:18:46Z). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261118-15: requirement into text, her 'Test must show' and 'Out of scope' bullets into test_must_show and out_of_scope; markdown bold dropped; relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private 81156ec, handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5.md (the round-4 ask and the wake summary only); not the PR diff, the tests or the text of AEC-R-pin-check@2. Implementation conformance: not assessed by the maintainer.", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-pin-check-source-clean", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Requirement: Source-checkout identity shall qualify only when HEAD matches the agreed pin and no tracked modification or non-ignored untracked file makes the checkout dirty.", "test_must_show": ["Clean pinned HEAD passes.", "Staged changes, unstaged changes and non-ignored untracked files fail.", "Ignored build artefacts alone do not fail."], "out_of_scope": "Developer overrides, sandboxing and inspection of ignored-file contents.", "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5--03c3b736dc5d.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-18T13:18:46Z). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261118-15: requirement into text, her 'Test must show' and 'Out of scope' bullets into test_must_show and out_of_scope; markdown bold dropped; relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private 81156ec, handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5.md (the round-4 ask and the wake summary only); not the PR diff, the tests or the text of AEC-R-pin-check@2. Implementation conformance: not assessed by the maintainer.", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-pin-check", "version": 3, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "aec pin-check [ROOT] exits 0 only when the local aec equals the Telosmith commit the repository's CI pins, and 1 with a one-line reason otherwise. Pins are read from the places repositories already use (each .github/workflows/*.yml|*.yaml line installing git+https://github.com/eraevous/Telosmith.git@<ref>, and tools/aec_upstream.json commit); every pin found must be a full 40-character commit SHA, and all must name the same commit: an abbreviated SHA, a tag, main or any branch fails. The local version is the commit from PEP 610 direct_url.json, or the HEAD of a clean Telosmith source checkout (no staged or unstaged change to a tracked file and no non-ignored untracked file anywhere in the checkout); anything else is indeterminate and fails. The pass condition is exact equality of the two commits; a requested revision recorded at install time is not used. Implements Kate's AEC-R-pin-check-consensus@1, AEC-R-pin-check-local-identity@1 and AEC-R-pin-check-source-clean@1, and is the equality check AEC-R-hook-line-pin-gate@1 (on Telosmith#89, not yet on main) asks the one-line hook to enforce. Out of scope: wiring it into the line launcher, defining a new pin-file format, installing the pinned release, inspecting ignored files.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check@2"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check-consensus@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check-local-identity@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check-source-clean@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/pin.py", "sha256": "2d6fe54147998f9cd3103be22ece1cb044d50bafa1b99567ae7e6db4a99bb11a", "locator": "q:`aec pin-check`: does the aec running here equal", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-pin-check", "version": 4, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "aec pin-check [ROOT] exits 0 only when the local aec equals the Telosmith commit the repository's CI pins, and 1 with a one-line reason otherwise. Pins are read from the places repositories already use (each .github/workflows/*.yml|*.yaml line installing git+https://github.com/eraevous/Telosmith.git@<ref>, and tools/aec_upstream.json commit); the workflow ref is the whole revision up to whitespace, a quote or pip's #egg= fragment, so a branch such as <sha>+hotfix is not read as its SHA prefix. Every pin found must be a full 40-character commit SHA, and all must name the same commit: an abbreviated SHA, a tag, main or any branch fails. The local version is the commit from PEP 610 direct_url.json, or the HEAD of a clean Telosmith source checkout (no staged or unstaged change to a tracked file, no non-ignored untracked file anywhere in the checkout, and no ignored file inside the package whose suffix the running interpreter imports, outside __pycache__); anything else is indeterminate and fails. The pass condition is exact equality of the two commits; a requested revision recorded at install time is not used. Implements Kate's AEC-R-pin-check-consensus@1, AEC-R-pin-check-local-identity@1 and AEC-R-pin-check-source-clean@1, and her round-5 replacement payload for ignored importable files except bytecode caches under __pycache__ (open with her), and is the equality check AEC-R-hook-line-pin-gate@1 (on Telosmith#89, not yet on main) asks the one-line hook to enforce. Out of scope: wiring it into the line launcher, suppressing bytecode generation (the launcher's job), defining a new pin-file format, installing the pinned release, what aec init writes.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check@3"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check-consensus@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check-local-identity@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check-source-clean@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/pin.py", "sha256": "f6469d115633b2e1bb93440a87fadb688a84508a9636bce2e7b090ccae3995ad", "locator": "q:`aec pin-check`: does the aec running here equal", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-pin-check-source-clean", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Requirement: Source-checkout identity shall qualify only when HEAD matches the agreed pin, no tracked modification or non-ignored untracked file exists, and ignored files cannot substitute executable content for the pinned aec source under the supported launch path; otherwise the check shall report why identity could not be established.", "test_must_show": ["Clean pinned HEAD passes.", "A different HEAD, staged changes, unstaged changes, and non-ignored untracked files fail qualification.", "Ignored build artefacts that cannot affect aec execution under the supported launch path do not fail qualification.", "Ignored sourceless bytecode and importable extension modules that can supply or replace aec executable content fail qualification.", "Existing source-associated bytecode caches fail qualification unless the supported launch path demonstrably prevents their execution or establishes that execution uses the pinned source instead.", "Refusal identifies the offending path or unsupported condition and does not delete or rewrite checkout files."], "out_of_scope": ["Developer overrides and sandboxing.", "Authenticating the agreed pin or the Git executable.", "Arbitrary hostile interpreters, import hooks, or concurrent filesystem changes.", "Inspection of ignored-file contents that cannot affect aec execution."], "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5--92f7359339fb.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-18T17:18:07Z). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261118-19: her YAML fields copied as given, folded scalars joined with single spaces; relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private 80e5dc8, handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5.md (the round-6 ask, which quoted @1 in full, and the wake summaries); not the PR diff or tests. Implementation conformance: not assessed by the maintainer.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check-source-clean@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-pin-check", "version": 5, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "aec pin-check [ROOT] exits 0 only when the local aec equals the Telosmith commit the repository's CI pins, and 1 with a one-line reason otherwise. Pins are read statically from the places repositories already use (each .github/workflows/*.yml|*.yaml line installing git+https://github.com/eraevous/Telosmith.git@<ref>, and tools/aec_upstream.json commit). In workflows, YAML and shell comments are ignored; a remaining line that names Telosmith's git URL without a static @<rev>, or a pip install built from a variable, fails as unreadable offline. The workflow ref is the whole revision up to whitespace, a quote or pip's #egg= fragment. Every pin found must be a full 40-character commit SHA, and all must name the same commit: an abbreviated SHA, a tag, main or any branch fails. The local version is the commit from PEP 610 direct_url.json, or the HEAD of a clean Telosmith source checkout: no staged or unstaged change to a tracked file, no non-ignored untracked file anywhere in the checkout, no ignored file inside the package whose suffix the running interpreter imports, and no bytecode cache under __pycache__ for the running interpreter's cache tag; with sys.pycache_prefix set the checkout does not qualify. Anything else is indeterminate and fails, with the reason and the offending paths; nothing is deleted. The pass condition is exact equality of the two commits; a requested revision recorded at install time is not used. Implements Kate's AEC-R-pin-check-consensus@1, AEC-R-pin-check-local-identity@1 and AEC-R-pin-check-source-clean@2, and is the equality check AEC-R-hook-line-pin-gate@1 (on Telosmith#89, not yet on main) asks the one-line hook to enforce. Out of scope: wiring it into the line launcher (which should run Python with -B), defining a new pin-file format, installing the pinned release, what aec init writes (AEC-R-init-full-commit-pin, a separate PR), shell constructs beyond comments and $-variables.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check@4"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check-consensus@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check-local-identity@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check-source-clean@2"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/pin.py", "sha256": "166ffd655ff6c02379d26c32f7fc761c566a8f90bf20865821727b962203e31e", "locator": "q:`aec pin-check`: does the aec running here equal", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-pin-check", "version": 6, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "aec pin-check [ROOT] exits 0 only when the local aec equals the Telosmith commit the repository's CI pins, and 1 with a one-line reason otherwise. Pins are read statically from the places repositories already use (each .github/workflows/*.yml|*.yaml line installing git+https://github.com/eraevous/Telosmith.git@<ref>, and tools/aec_upstream.json commit). In workflows, YAML and shell comments and display text (name: and description: lines) are ignored; a remaining line that names Telosmith's git URL without a static @<rev>, or a pip install built from a variable, fails as unreadable offline. The workflow ref is the whole revision up to whitespace, a quote or pip's #egg= fragment. Every pin found must be a full 40-character commit SHA, and all must name the same commit: an abbreviated SHA, a tag, main or any branch fails. The local version is the commit from PEP 610 direct_url.json, or the HEAD of a clean Telosmith source checkout: no staged or unstaged change to a tracked file, no non-ignored untracked file anywhere in the checkout, no ignored file inside the package whose suffix the running interpreter imports, and no bytecode cache under __pycache__ for the running interpreter's cache tag; with sys.pycache_prefix set the checkout does not qualify. Anything else is indeterminate and fails, with the reason and the offending paths; nothing is deleted. The pass condition is exact equality of the two commits; a requested revision recorded at install time is not used. Implements Kate's AEC-R-pin-check-consensus@1, AEC-R-pin-check-local-identity@1 and AEC-R-pin-check-source-clean@2, and is the equality check AEC-R-hook-line-pin-gate@1 (on Telosmith#89, not yet on main) asks the one-line hook to enforce. Out of scope: tampering with the installation or checkout before aec starts (the check runs inside the aec it checks; a defence has to verify from outside, before importing it), wiring it into the line launcher (which should run Python with -B), defining a new pin-file format, installing the pinned release, what aec init writes (AEC-R-init-full-commit-pin, a separate PR), shell constructs beyond comments and $-variables.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check@5"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check-consensus@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check-local-identity@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check-source-clean@2"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/pin.py", "sha256": "4bcac9cdc76c2c2321779d5323a3e8a6e7aaf203781c4d8cf8ebd133e615c6ea", "locator": "q:`aec pin-check`: does the aec running here equal", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-D-pin-check-scope", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "subject": "aec-scope", "status": "accepted", "decided_by": "AU-zach", "text": "aec pin-check reads the pin only from tools/aec_upstream.json (commit, a full 40-character SHA; a symlink, missing or unreadable file fails) and no longer scans workflow files; and only a pip install from git with a recorded commit (PEP 610) counts as the local version, so a source checkout or editable install is indeterminate and fails. Reason: six review rounds on Telosmith#90 found new ways to steer a line reader over workflow YAML and shell, and code in a writable source checkout runs before the check and can forge its answer. Narrows Kate's AEC-R-pin-check-consensus@1 (workflow pins are no longer discovered) and AEC-R-pin-check-local-identity@1 and AEC-R-pin-check-source-clean@2 (source-checkout identity no longer qualifies); those records stand as written and their next versions are Kate's to append. Follow-ups, not in this decision: aec init writing tools/aec_upstream.json, and a CI-side check that CI installs the commit the file names.", "quote": "Pin file only (Recommended); Reject source checkouts (Recommended)", "origin": "Zach, answering two option questions in the claude:aec session on Telosmith#90 review notes, 2026-11-18 ~22:25Z (reading: explicit, chosen options)", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-pin-check", "version": 7, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "aec pin-check [ROOT] exits 0 only when the local aec equals the commit in ROOT/tools/aec_upstream.json, and 1 with a one-line reason otherwise (AEC-D-pin-check-scope@1). The pin file is the only pin source; workflow files are not read. It fails when the file is missing, a symlink (dangling or not), not a regular file, unreadable JSON, has no commit, or its commit is not a full 40-character SHA (abbreviated, tag, branch or suffixed refs). The local version is the commit from PEP 610 direct_url.json of a pip install from git; a source checkout or editable install is indeterminate and fails. The pass condition is exact equality of the two commits. Out of scope: tampering with an installed environment, whether CI installs the commit the file names (a CI-side check), aec init writing the pin file, and wiring the check into the line launcher.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check@6"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-pin-check-scope@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/pin.py", "sha256": "13d79144d4591877798badcd0190fb52c8ee78c4b412b505317d3826560bf169", "locator": "q:`aec pin-check`: does the aec running here equal", "for": "text"}]}
