{"id": "AEC-R-pin-check-local-identity", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Pin-check shall report a local-version match only for a non-editable pip installation from Git whose PEP 610 metadata supplies a commit identity matching the canonical pin; neither a source-checkout HEAD nor an editable installation qualifies.", "test_must_show": ["A qualifying installed Git commit matching the pin succeeds; a different commit does not.", "Missing, malformed, or commit-less PEP 610 metadata cannot establish a match.", "An editable installation cannot establish a match, even with matching Git metadata.", "A checkout alone cannot establish a match, whether clean or dirty and whether its HEAD matches or differs."], "out_of_scope": ["Checkout cleanliness as an acceptance criterion.", "Package-version strings or checkout HEAD as substitute identity evidence.", "Independent attestation of installation history beyond the accepted metadata."], "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5--f2a0bfab42ac.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-18T22:28:11Z). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261119-01: her quoted requirement into text (outer quotation marks dropped), her 'Test must show' and 'Out of scope' bullets into test_must_show and out_of_scope; markdown dropped; relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private f5b464e, handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5.md (the round-7b ask, which summarised AEC-D-pin-check-scope@1 and quoted the overtaken phrases, and the wake summaries); not the PR diff or tests. Kate: 'No diff or test results for 14c200f were supplied.' Implementation conformance: not assessed by the maintainer.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check-local-identity@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-pin-check-scope@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}]}
