{"id": "AEC-R-pin-check", "version": 8, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "aec pin-check [ROOT] exits 0 only when the local aec equals the commit in ROOT/tools/aec_upstream.json, and 1 with a one-line reason otherwise (AEC-D-pin-check-scope@1). The pin file is the only pin source; workflow files are not read. It fails when the file is missing, a symlink (dangling or not), not a regular file, unreadable JSON, has no commit, or its commit is not a full 40-character SHA (abbreviated, tag, branch or suffixed refs). The local version is the commit from PEP 610 direct_url.json of a non-editable pip install from git (vcs_info.vcs is \"git\", the commit is a full 40-character SHA, and the metadata belongs to the aec actually running); a source checkout, an editable install, another version-control system, or missing or malformed metadata is indeterminate and fails. The pass condition is exact equality of the two commits. Out of scope: tampering with an installed environment, whether CI installs the commit the file names (a CI-side check), aec init writing the pin file, and wiring the check into the line launcher.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check@7"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-pin-check-scope@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check-consensus@2"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check-local-identity@2"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/pin.py", "sha256": "13d79144d4591877798badcd0190fb52c8ee78c4b412b505317d3826560bf169", "locator": "q:`aec pin-check`: does the aec running here equal", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-init-full-commit-pin", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Requirement: Whenever aec init generates a Git-based Telosmith pin, it shall write the full commit object ID corresponding to the selected revision, rather than a branch, tag, abbreviated ID, or other movable reference, and shall fail with a diagnostic without writing an unresolved pin if that commit cannot be established.", "test_must_show": ["A selected branch, tag, or abbreviated commit resolves to and is written as the full commit object ID.", "An annotated tag resolves to its commit, not its tag-object ID.", "An already-full commit ID is preserved.", "Generated consumers use the same resolved commit wherever init repeats that pin.", "Unresolvable, ambiguous, or non-commit revisions produce a diagnostic and no unresolved or placeholder pin."], "out_of_scope": ["Selecting or approving the Telosmith revision.", "Authenticating upstream commits or release signatures.", "Updating existing repositories or implementing a pin-bump bot."], "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5--92f7359339fb.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-18T17:18:07Z). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261119-15 from her YAML block (folded text joined into one line); relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5.md round-5 ask (a summary of Telosmith#90 and its review state); not this PR's diff or tests. Implementation conformance: not assessed by the maintainer.", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-init-full-commit-pin-impl", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "When aec init writes the hook and CI snippets, it resolves the Telosmith revision it pins to a full 40-character commit before writing anything, and uses that commit in the CI snippet and in every next step that names the install. A full commit is kept as given; a branch or tag is resolved with git ls-remote against the Telosmith source (an annotated tag gives its peeled commit; a name that is both a tag and a branch on different commits is refused); an abbreviated commit is resolved only in a Telosmith checkout with git rev-parse REV^{commit}. Offline, no git, an unknown, ambiguous or non-commit revision raises PinResolutionError naming the reason, and init writes nothing (the CLI exits non-zero); --no-hooks needs no resolution. Not checked: whether a remote tag or branch points at a commit rather than another object type (ls-remote does not say), and the Telosmith CI attribute outside init, which still uses install_ref.", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-init-full-commit-pin@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/init.py", "sha256": "fd58ec9b71c3b4540b3580e71452f6d4784fd95f19a6827417bb6505a2d96be3", "locator": "q:The full commit object ID for `rev`, or PinResolutionError", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-init-full-commit-pin-impl", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "When aec init writes the hook and CI snippets, it resolves the Telosmith revision it pins to a full 40-character commit before writing anything, and uses that commit in the CI snippet and in every next step that names the install. A full commit is kept as given; a branch or tag is resolved with git ls-remote against the Telosmith source (an annotated tag gives its peeled commit; a name that is both a tag and a branch on different commits is refused), and the chosen id is then fetched shallow into a throwaway repository and accepted only if git reports it is a commit (a tag naming a tree or blob is refused); an abbreviated commit is resolved only in a Telosmith checkout with git rev-parse REV^{commit}. Offline, no git, an unknown, ambiguous or non-commit revision raises PinResolutionError naming the reason, and init writes nothing (the CLI exits non-zero); --no-hooks needs no resolution. Not covered: the Telosmith CI attribute outside init, which still uses install_ref.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-init-full-commit-pin-impl@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-init-full-commit-pin@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/init.py", "sha256": "0b6717da6d9538e1bea204649241f91edd45a134a6c38bf53bd4b0d9a7c49570", "locator": "q:The full commit object ID for `rev`, or PinResolutionError", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-init-full-commit-pin-impl", "version": 3, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "When aec init writes the hook and CI snippets, it resolves the Telosmith revision it pins to a full 40-character commit before writing anything, and uses that commit in the CI snippet and in every next step that names the install. Every result is a git-confirmed commit: a full id is kept unchanged only after git cat-file reports it is a commit (in the Telosmith checkout when the id is that checkout's HEAD, so an unpushed HEAD still works; otherwise fetched shallow from the Telosmith source into a throwaway repository); a branch or tag is resolved with git ls-remote (an annotated tag gives its peeled commit; a name that is both a tag and a branch on different commits is refused) and the chosen id is checked the same way at the source; an abbreviated commit is resolved only in a Telosmith checkout with git rev-parse REV^{commit}. Offline, no git, a missing object, or an unknown, ambiguous or non-commit revision raises PinResolutionError naming the reason, and init writes nothing (the CLI exits non-zero); --no-hooks needs no resolution. Not covered: the Telosmith CI attribute outside init, which still uses install_ref.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-init-full-commit-pin-impl@2"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-init-full-commit-pin@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/init.py", "sha256": "093dad23106664a8d91e4c7742c0a118bfab43ffd1785ad01573d70a643324ec", "locator": "q:The full commit object ID for `rev`, or PinResolutionError", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-init-full-commit-pin-impl", "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "version": 4, "text": "When aec init writes the hook and CI snippets, it resolves the Telosmith revision it pins to a full 40-character commit before writing anything, and uses that commit in the CI snippet and in every next step that names the install. Every result is a git-confirmed commit: a full id is kept unchanged only after git cat-file reports it is a commit (in the Telosmith checkout when the id is that checkout's HEAD, so an unpushed HEAD still works; otherwise fetched shallow from the Telosmith source into a throwaway repository); a branch or tag is resolved with git ls-remote (an annotated tag gives its peeled commit; a name that is both a tag and a branch on different commits is refused) and the chosen id is checked the same way at the source; an abbreviated commit is resolved only in a Telosmith checkout with git rev-parse REV^{commit}. Offline, no git, a missing object, or an unknown, ambiguous or non-commit revision raises PinResolutionError naming the reason, keeping git's own message (fetch or cat-file stderr, a timeout, git missing) apart from a non-commit object type, and init writes nothing (the CLI exits non-zero); --no-hooks needs no resolution. Not covered: the Telosmith CI attribute outside init, which still uses install_ref. When the CI snippet already exists, init keeps it and its next steps say so instead of claiming it pins the newly resolved commit.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-init-full-commit-pin-impl@3"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-init-full-commit-pin@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/init.py", "sha256": "c236ba936688b749335570f086b0fce6437623455a524fd52d84c411b12d77fe", "locator": "q:The full commit object ID for `rev`, or PinResolutionError", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-D-repo-config", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "subject": "aec-scope", "status": "proposed", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@3"}], "text": "Proposed (HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC, under DEC-256): Telosmith's per-repository configuration lives in .aec/config.toml, not in [tool.telosmith] of pyproject.toml, because six of the thirteen repositories with .aec/ that the lane can read have no pyproject.toml. Without the file every command keeps today's defaults on every supported Python; with it, Python 3.11+ reads it with tomllib and Python 3.10 stops with a message naming the file, since Telosmith has no runtime dependencies and writes no TOML parser of its own. Unknown keys are an error. Not decided here: the exact keys (they come with the item-1 change and its maintainer records), raising the Python floor to 3.11, and folding .aec/sources.json into the config.", "anchors": [{"path": "docs/integrations/dev-kit-base.md", "sha256": "2c61d2c07bd4e9a62963f04380989ad0c3eabc01b2a18afc1af02b7916d9c2a2", "locator": "q:## The one call for Zach now: where the per-repository config lives", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-D-repo-config", "version": 2, "type": "decision", "subject": "aec-scope", "status": "accepted", "decided_by": "AU-zach", "quote": "Decided as aec/config.json", "origin": "Zach, issue comment 7042524672 on Telosmith#94, 2026-11-20T14:49:16Z (eraevous account, not via an app; reading: explicit, chosen option; 'aec/config.json' read as .aec/config.json, the JSON option the PR listed)", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@3"}], "text": "Telosmith's per-repository configuration lives in .aec/config.json (supersedes the proposed .aec/config.toml of @1). It is read with the standard-library json module on every supported Python, so 3.10 needs no special handling. Without the file every command keeps today's defaults; unknown keys are an error. Not decided here: the exact keys (they come with the item-1 change and its maintainer records) and folding .aec/sources.json into the config.", "anchors": [{"path": "docs/integrations/dev-kit-base.md", "sha256": "e30ed3129b267422d0c1d0c82e95eea92edff82b052731cff51b095a55cf9848", "locator": "q:## Decided: `.aec/config.json`", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-a2a-card-impl", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "aec a2a builds and checks an A2A 1.0 Agent Card for a Telosmith-based project (DEC-256 item 5, second slice, an experiment under DEC-200). aec.a2a.build_card returns a card with name, description, supportedInterfaces (one entry: url, protocolBinding, protocolVersion 1.0), version, capabilities, defaultInputModes, defaultOutputModes and skills, never the 0.3 top-level url, preferredTransport or protocolVersion, and raises CardError naming every problem. aec.a2a.validate_card returns the problems that stop a value being a 1.0 card (missing required fields, empty strings or lists, non-http(s) URLs, non-boolean capabilities, skills without tags, repeated skill ids, an incomplete provider) and never raises. aec a2a card prints the card or writes it with -o, never overwriting; aec a2a check exits 0 only for a valid card, else 1 with one line per problem. Not covered: serving or signing the card, security schemes, the extended card, A2A task handling, the Agent Skills folder and the authority socket.", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@3"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/a2a.py", "sha256": "461b5395ae16a6e87697071efc85e2ccdbed15291b5e981d661a87e11165c771", "locator": "q:A2A Agent Card for a Telosmith-based project", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-a2a-card-contract", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Requirement: Generated cards shall conform to an explicitly pinned A2A 1.0 JSON wire contract and describe the configured project.", "test_must_show": ["An independent schema or implementation accepts a generated fixture; required fields, nested structures, defaults and optional fields have the specified wire representation; generation omits obsolete 0.3 top-level fields."], "out_of_scope": ["Serving, signing, task execution and support for other protocol revisions."], "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC--508d054dce4f.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-20T13:21:29Z; marked [opinion] by her). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261120-13 from her Proposed records list; relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC.md round-3 ask (a behaviour summary of Telosmith#96 at e14e93c); not the diff, test bodies, normative schema or independent-client results. Implementation conformance: not assessed by the maintainer.", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-a2a-card-validation", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Requirement: Validation shall return actionable, field-addressed problems for every detected contract violation without raising on JSON-representable input, and generation shall reject invalid inputs with `CardError`.", "test_must_show": ["Root scalars/null/lists, incorrect nested types, missing fields, empty values, invalid URLs, non-boolean capabilities, duplicate skill IDs and incomplete providers produce diagnostics rather than exceptions; multiple independent defects are reported together."], "out_of_scope": ["Network reachability, endpoint authenticity and proof that advertised capabilities work."], "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC--508d054dce4f.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-20T13:21:29Z; marked [opinion] by her). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261120-13 from her Proposed records list; relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC.md round-3 ask (a behaviour summary of Telosmith#96 at e14e93c); not the diff, test bodies, normative schema or independent-client results. Implementation conformance: not assessed by the maintainer.", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-a2a-card-cli", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Requirement: The CLI shall emit a valid card or a clear failure, preserve existing output files, and report check success only for cards satisfying the pinned contract.", "test_must_show": ["Stdout contains only parseable card JSON on success; file output round-trips through validation; an existing destination remains byte-for-byte unchanged; malformed JSON, invalid cards and unreadable files yield nonzero exits with diagnostics."], "out_of_scope": ["Publication, discovery hosting and deployment."], "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC--508d054dce4f.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-20T13:21:29Z; marked [opinion] by her). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261120-13 from her Proposed records list; relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC.md round-3 ask (a behaviour summary of Telosmith#96 at e14e93c); not the diff, test bodies, normative schema or independent-client results. Implementation conformance: not assessed by the maintainer.", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-a2a-card-claims", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Requirement: Card declarations and documentation shall distinguish configured capability claims, structural validation and demonstrated interoperability.", "test_must_show": ["Explicit skills and capability flags survive generation unchanged; documentation does not equate checker success with working endpoints or item-6 compatibility."], "out_of_scope": ["Automatic MCP-to-A2A semantic equivalence and executing advertised skills in this slice."], "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC--508d054dce4f.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-20T13:21:29Z; marked [opinion] by her). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261120-13 from her Proposed records list; relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC.md round-3 ask (a behaviour summary of Telosmith#96 at e14e93c); not the diff, test bodies, normative schema or independent-client results. Implementation conformance: not assessed by the maintainer.", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-init-writes-pin-file-impl", "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "version": 1, "text": "When aec init writes hooks with --hook-style line, it also writes tools/aec_upstream.json naming the same full commit the CI snippet pins (with the Telosmith repo URL and a _doc line), so the line hook and aec pin-check have the pin they require. It never overwrites an existing file or a dangling symlink at that path (the path is reported as kept and the next step says to check it names the resolved commit), never writes through a tools/ that is a symlink or not a directory (nothing is written and the next step says so), and writes nothing when the commit cannot be established. The inline default and --no-hooks write no pin file. Not covered: keeping the pin file and the CI job on the same commit after init; the CI job does not read the pin file.", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-hook-line-pin-gate@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-pin-check-scope@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-init-full-commit-pin-impl@4"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/init.py", "sha256": "0d766846857727a02b199382c14011df60f91acf60350312af9cd1e281624bd5", "locator": "q:The pin file `aec init --hook-style line` writes", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-init-line-pin-bootstrap", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5--a2c9ed01d70c.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-19T21:19:54Z). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261119-21: her Requirement into text, her 'Test must show' and 'Out of scope' bullets into test_must_show and out_of_scope; markdown (backticks) dropped; relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5.md round-13 ask: a prose description of the behaviour, the rules as built and the implementer record text; no diff, test source or test output for 8509a0b. Kate: no semantic blocker in the described scope; implementation unassessed.", "text": "When init creates line-style hooks and can resolve the upstream full commit, it must create an absent tools/aec_upstream.json under a safe tools directory, containing _doc, repo https://github.com/eraevous/Telosmith, and the same full commit used in the generated CI snippet.", "test_must_show": ["Fresh line-style init produces parseable JSON with those fields.", "Pin-file commit equals the CI snippet’s full commit.", "Default/explicit inline and --no-hooks create no pin file."], "out_of_scope": ["Installed-package provenance enforcement, already assigned to the hook gate; ongoing pin/CI synchronization."], "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-hook-line-pin-gate@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-pin-check-scope@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-init-pin-preservation", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5--a2c9ed01d70c.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-19T21:19:54Z). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261119-21: her Requirement into text, her 'Test must show' and 'Out of scope' bullets into test_must_show and out_of_scope; markdown (backticks) dropped; relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5.md round-13 ask: a prose description of the behaviour, the rules as built and the implementer record text; no diff, test source or test output for 8509a0b. Kate: no semantic blocker in the described scope; implementation unassessed.", "text": "Init must preserve an existing pin file or pin-path symlink without writing through it, and must not write the pin file through a symlinked or non-directory tools path, while providing the corresponding corrective next step.", "test_must_show": ["Existing file bytes remain unchanged.", "Live and dangling pin-path symlinks remain unchanged; their targets are neither modified nor created.", "Symlinked/non-directory tools paths cause no pin write or target mutation.", "Preserved pin entries prompt checking against the resolved commit; unsafe tools paths warn that the line hook will refuse until a regular pin file exists."], "out_of_scope": ["Repairing existing paths, validating preserved contents, concurrent filesystem mutation guarantees."], "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-init-line-pin-bootstrap@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-init-unresolved-pin-no-write", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5--a2c9ed01d70c.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-19T21:19:54Z). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261119-21: her Requirement into text, her 'Test must show' and 'Out of scope' bullets into test_must_show and out_of_scope; markdown (backticks) dropped; relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5.md round-13 ask: a prose description of the behaviour, the rules as built and the implementer record text; no diff, test source or test output for 8509a0b. Kate: no semantic blocker in the described scope; implementation unassessed.", "text": "If init cannot resolve the required full commit, it must perform no filesystem writes.", "test_must_show": ["An unresolved-commit invocation leaves the fixture filesystem unchanged, including hooks, CI configuration, .aec/, and pin-file paths."], "out_of_scope": ["Commit-resolution policy and network availability."], "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-init-full-commit-pin@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-init-writes-pin-file-impl", "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "version": 2, "text": "When aec init writes hooks with --hook-style line, it also writes tools/aec_upstream.json naming the same full commit the CI snippet pins (with the Telosmith repo URL and a _doc line), so the line hook and aec pin-check have the pin they require. It never overwrites an existing file or a live or dangling symlink at that path (the path is reported as kept, the target is neither changed nor created, and the next step says to check it names the resolved commit), never writes through a tools/ that is a symlink or not a directory (nothing is written and the next step says the line hook will refuse), and writes nothing at all when the commit cannot be established. The inline default and --no-hooks write no pin file. Equality with the CI snippet holds at generation only: neither file governs the other afterwards, and the CI job does not read the pin file.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-init-writes-pin-file-impl@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-init-line-pin-bootstrap@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-init-pin-preservation@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-init-unresolved-pin-no-write@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-init-full-commit-pin-impl@4"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/init.py", "sha256": "91764c7a358d90d4333f9f78697e79494cd740a94d0a76d04c23b09a394040f0", "locator": "q:The pin file `aec init --hook-style line` writes", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-init-writes-pin-file-impl", "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "version": 3, "text": "When aec init writes hooks with --hook-style line, it also writes tools/aec_upstream.json naming the same full commit the CI snippet pins (with the Telosmith repo URL and a _doc line), so aec pin-check, and the line hook once its launcher has the pre-import pin gate (Telosmith#92), have the pin they read. The _doc line and next steps say that enforcement by the hook depends on that gate and never claim it unconditionally (Copilot on #93). It never overwrites an existing file or a live or dangling symlink at that path (the path is reported as kept, the target is neither changed nor created, and the next step says to check it names the resolved commit), never writes through a tools/ that is a symlink or not a directory (nothing is written and the next step says pin-check will fail), and writes nothing at all when the commit cannot be established. The inline default and --no-hooks write no pin file. Equality with the CI snippet holds at generation only: neither file governs the other afterwards, and the CI job does not read the pin file.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-init-writes-pin-file-impl@2"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-init-line-pin-bootstrap@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-init-pin-preservation@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-init-unresolved-pin-no-write@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-init-full-commit-pin-impl@4"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/init.py", "sha256": "ef0e0bb07a844bea300d7e5fde936bf2b52b457de436b72bca4b4ed1d06aaa5c", "locator": "q:The pin file `aec init --hook-style line` writes", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-hook-launcher-preimport", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Before importing or executing Telosmith from a source checkout, the line launcher must use a verifier outside that checkout and its control to establish that the code to be executed matches the configured pin, rejecting additional importable content and preventing substitution between verification and execution; otherwise it must report the failure and exit 1 without executing checkout code.", "test_must_show": ["A clean checkout matching the pin runs successfully.", "A wrong revision, modified tracked module, or ignored/untracked shadow package is rejected before any checkout-controlled startup side effect occurs. Include the reported src/aec/records/__init__.py case.", "Checkout-controlled working-directory files, environment import paths, and symlinks cannot replace the verifier or redirect verified imports.", "A change after verification cannot introduce executed code. Execute an isolated verified snapshot, or demonstrate an equivalent protection.", "Missing verification capability fails closed with a diagnostic."], "out_of_scope": ["Authenticating who authorized the configured pin.", "Compromise of the trusted launcher, verifier, interpreter, OS, or pin configuration.", "Proving that correctly pinned code is benign.", "Replacing the existing installed-package integrity policy."], "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5--7e1b420ae7f1.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-18T21:20:40Z). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261119-19: her Sentence into text, her 'What a test must show' bullets (nested bullets joined to their parent) into test_must_show, her 'Out of scope' bullets into out_of_scope; markdown dropped; relations added by the transcriber. Written before AEC-D-pin-check-scope@1, under which no source checkout qualifies, so the line never executes one; her next version is asked for in round 12.", "shown": "relay-kit-private handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5.md round-7 ask (the Codex security P2 on Telosmith#90 and the two options); not this PR's diff or tests. Kate: 'I have the reported attack and requirement summary, not head 0ec4f9c, its diff, or tests. Implementation conformance is not assessed.'", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-hook-line-pin-gate@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-hook-line", "version": 3, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "aec init --hook-style line writes a project hook whose settings text holds only the launcher and a pre-import gate, which calls aec hook project, the hook body shipped in the package. Before any aec code runs, the gate (one python3 -I -B process started from /, with the filtered PYTHONPATH entries appended after the interpreter's own path) requires commit in tools/aec_upstream.json to be a full 40-character SHA in a regular file, finds aec without importing it, and accepts it only when it belongs to an installed telosmith distribution whose PEP 610 metadata is a non-editable git install of exactly that commit, outside the project; it then loads that same spec and runs the body in the same process. A missing or malformed pin, no importable aec, a source checkout, an editable install, another commit or version-control system, a shadowing aec earlier on the path, or a pinned aec without hook project each exits 1 with one line saying which. On the same checkout with a pinned install it exits as the inline hook does: 0 when quiet, 1 when a step could not run, 2 with a report for the agent; a symlink at .aec, the records file or either output is refused. inline stays the default. Out of scope: tampering with the installed environment (the user-level hook verifies RECORD), aec init writing the pin file, and replacing any repository's existing hook.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-hook-line@2"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-hook-launcher-preimport@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-hook-line-pin-gate@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check-local-identity@2"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-pin-check-scope@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:src.aec.userhook.project_run"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-hook-safe-path@6"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/init.py", "sha256": "b976acc609eef0fdeba3b11e7b544d41818aa76a7eae64b3f2c4daabacb048f7", "locator": "q:HOOK_LINE_GATE = (", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-hook-launcher-preimport", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Before executing any aec code, the line-hook launcher must validate the project's full lowercase 40-hex commit pin and establish that the selected aec package is outside the project and belongs to a non-editable installed Telosmith distribution whose PEP 610 metadata identifies Git and that exact commit, otherwise refusing without executing the rejected package.", "test_must_show": ["A qualifying installation executes successfully.", "Missing or invalid pins, checkout/editable candidates, absent provenance, and mismatched provenance fail closed.", "Rejected candidates' package initializers and shadow modules never execute.", "Project/PYTHONPATH startup and standard-library shadows cannot execute before validation."], "out_of_scope": ["Verifying a source checkout as an acceptable alternative.", "Authenticating installed metadata against deliberate forgery.", "Snapshotting installed files or preventing installed-environment tampering.", "Replacing the existing installed-package integrity policy."], "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5--89193914a6b7.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-19T19:26:37Z). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261119-19: her Requirement into text, her 'What a test must show' and 'Out of scope' bullets into test_must_show and out_of_scope; markdown dropped; relations added by the transcriber. The same ask was answered twice (an earlier reply, HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5--2d1ae5877b87 at 19:21:51Z, proposed a differently worded @2 with the same substance); this is the later one.", "shown": "relay-kit-private handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5.md round-12 ask: the gate text exactly, the settings-line outline, and the test list with reported results; not the full @1, AEC-R-pin-check@8, the settings command, the path filter, the test source or the PR diff. Kate: no blocker against @2; not a whole-PR approval.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-hook-launcher-preimport@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-pin-check-scope@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-hook-line-pin-gate@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-hook-line", "version": 4, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "aec init --hook-style line writes a project hook whose settings text holds only the launcher and a pre-import gate, which calls aec hook project, the hook body shipped in the package. Before any aec code runs, the gate (one python3 -I -B process started from /, with the filtered PYTHONPATH entries appended after the interpreter's own path) requires commit in tools/aec_upstream.json to be a full 40-character SHA in a regular file, finds aec without importing it, and accepts it only when it belongs to an installed telosmith distribution whose PEP 610 metadata is a non-editable git install of exactly that commit, outside the project; it then loads that same spec and runs the body in the same process. A missing or malformed pin, no importable aec, a source checkout, an editable install, another commit or version-control system, a shadowing aec earlier on the path, or a pinned aec without hook project each exits 1 with one line saying which. On the same checkout with a pinned install it exits as the inline hook does: 0 when quiet, 1 when a step could not run, 2 with a report for the agent; a symlink at .aec, the records file or either output is refused. inline stays the default. Out of scope: tampering with the installed environment (the user-level hook verifies RECORD), aec init writing the pin file, and replacing any repository's existing hook.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-hook-line@3"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-hook-launcher-preimport@2"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-hook-line-pin-gate@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check-local-identity@2"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-pin-check-scope@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:src.aec.userhook.project_run"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to"