{"id": "AEC-R-mcp-skeleton-impl", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "aec mcp serves a repository's records over the Model Context Protocol on stdio (DEC-256 item 5, first slice, an experiment under DEC-200). aec.mcp.McpServer is a standard-library JSON-RPC 2.0 server that a Telosmith-based project registers its own tools on: it answers initialize (echoing a supported revision among 2024-11-05, 2025-03-26, 2025-06-18 and 2025-11-25, else the newest), ping, tools/list and tools/call; never answers a notification; refuses batches and malformed requests with -32600, unknown methods with -32601, unknown tools and non-object params or arguments with -32602, and unparseable lines with -32700; and reports a tool's refusal or exception as a result with isError rather than a protocol error. telosmith_server(root) adds three read-only tools over .aec/records.jsonl, read fresh on each call: records_list, record_get and records_check; every record result carries a notice that record text is untrusted data. Not covered: resources, prompts, HTTP transport, the A2A Agent Card, the Agent Skills folder and the authority socket (later slices).", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@3"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/mcp.py", "sha256": "2be51223020ea46cc33342ca8c7d1cb967ff8d801b5bc43280daf243eb2b4944", "locator": "q:small, standard-library MCP server over stdio", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-mcp-skeleton-impl", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "aec mcp serves a repository's records over the Model Context Protocol on stdio (DEC-256 item 5, first slice, an experiment under DEC-200). aec.mcp.McpServer is a standard-library JSON-RPC 2.0 server that a Telosmith-based project registers its own tools on: it answers initialize (echoing a supported revision among 2024-11-05, 2025-03-26, 2025-06-18 and 2025-11-25, else the newest), ping, tools/list and tools/call; never answers a notification; refuses batches and malformed requests with -32600, unknown methods with -32601, unknown or non-string tool names and non-object params or arguments with -32602, and unparseable lines with -32700; reports a tool's refusal or exception as a result with isError rather than a protocol error; and answers an exception in its own dispatch with -32603 for that request instead of ending the session. telosmith_server(root) adds three read-only tools over .aec/records.jsonl, read fresh on each call: records_list, record_get and records_check; every record result carries a notice that record text is untrusted data. Not covered: resources, prompts, HTTP transport, the A2A Agent Card, the Agent Skills folder and the authority socket (later slices).", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-mcp-skeleton-impl@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@3"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/mcp.py", "sha256": "51197aa1ea4bc687c0aa2ed2dc1464e7a7f48ac87f6e87cea143c79271317a0b", "locator": "q:small, standard-library MCP server over stdio", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-mcp-protocol", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Requirement: The stdio server shall implement the advertised MCP revisions’ applicable initialization, lifecycle, tool-discovery, tool-call and JSON-RPC error semantics without contaminating stdout with diagnostics.", "test_must_show": ["An independent client initializes, sends the initialized notification, lists tools and calls one successfully.", "Each advertised revision works; unsupported-version negotiation is exercised.", "Request IDs are preserved; valid notifications receive no response; malformed messages, batches and unknown methods produce the specified errors.", "Diagnostics go to stderr, and a recoverable bad message does not prevent the next valid request."], "out_of_scope": ["HTTP, resources, prompts and capabilities not advertised."], "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC--85e04e3d8ba1.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-20T03:18:32Z; marked [opinion] by her). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261120-03 from her Proposed records list; relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC.md round-2 ask (a behaviour summary of Telosmith#95 at 71323e6); not the diff, test bodies or results. Implementation conformance: not assessed by the maintainer.", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-mcp-tool-contract", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Requirement: Registered tools shall expose deterministic, documented names and input/output contracts, with protocol errors distinguished from tool-execution failures.", "test_must_show": ["A project-defined example tool is discoverable and callable using only its advertised contract.", "Invalid arguments are rejected before executing the handler.", "Unknown tools, invalid params, refusals and exceptions follow the documented error mapping.", "Duplicate registration cannot silently replace a built-in tool; exception responses do not expose tracebacks or environment details."], "out_of_scope": ["Sandboxing arbitrary project handlers or making project-defined tools read-only."], "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC--85e04e3d8ba1.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-20T03:18:32Z; marked [opinion] by her). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261120-03 from her Proposed records list; relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC.md round-2 ask (a behaviour summary of Telosmith#95 at 71323e6); not the diff, test bodies or results. Implementation conformance: not assessed by the maintainer.", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-mcp-record-reads", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Requirement: The three built-in record tools shall return fresh, read-only repository-record views with explicitly defined selection, ordering, version and failure semantics.", "test_must_show": ["Latest/all versions, combined filters, deterministic ordering, limit boundaries, exact/versioned lookup and newer-version indication.", "A file change between calls is visible; calls leave repository files unchanged.", "Missing or malformed records and missing IDs have documented outcomes.", "`records_check` matches the corresponding local check for the same input, with the exclusion of edges explicit."], "out_of_scope": ["Record mutation, edge checking and config integration not implemented in this slice."], "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC--85e04e3d8ba1.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-20T03:18:32Z; marked [opinion] by her). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261120-03 from her Proposed records list; relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC.md round-2 ask (a behaviour summary of Telosmith#95 at 71323e6); not the diff, test bodies or results. Implementation conformance: not assessed by the maintainer.", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-mcp-record-trust", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Requirement: Every response containing record-derived text shall identify that text as untrusted data rather than instructions or authority.", "test_must_show": ["The notice survives list, get and check paths, including findings or failures that quote record text.", "Instruction-like record content is returned as data and never executed by the server."], "out_of_scope": ["Guaranteeing that a consuming model obeys the notice."], "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC--85e04e3d8ba1.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-20T03:18:32Z; marked [opinion] by her). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261120-03 from her Proposed records list; relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC.md round-2 ask (a behaviour summary of Telosmith#95 at 71323e6); not the diff, test bodies or results. Implementation conformance: not assessed by the maintainer.", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-mcp-skeleton-impl", "version": 3, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "aec mcp serves a repository's records over the Model Context Protocol on stdio (DEC-256 item 5, first slice, an experiment under DEC-200). aec.mcp.McpServer is a standard-library JSON-RPC 2.0 server that a Telosmith-based project registers its own tools on: it answers initialize (echoing a supported revision among 2024-11-05, 2025-03-26, 2025-06-18 and 2025-11-25, else the newest), ping, tools/list and tools/call; never answers a notification; refuses batches and malformed requests with -32600, unknown methods with -32601, unknown or non-string tool names and non-object params or arguments with -32602, and unparseable lines with -32700; checks a call's arguments against the tool's inputSchema before the handler runs (top-level required; per property type, enum and minimum; additionalProperties false when declared) and reports any problem as a result with isError, never running the handler; reports a tool's refusal as a result with isError, and an exception as a result with isError naming only the exception type (its message, which can carry paths, goes to stderr); and answers an exception in its own dispatch with -32603 for that request instead of ending the session. telosmith_server(root) adds three read-only tools over .aec/records.jsonl, read fresh on each call: records_list, record_get and records_check; every record result carries a notice that record text is untrusted data. Not covered: resources, prompts, HTTP transport, the A2A Agent Card, the Agent Skills folder and the authority socket (later slices). Closes gaps 1 to 3 the implementer found against Kate's AEC-R-mcp-tool-contract@1 and AEC-R-mcp-record-reads@1: argument validation, no environment details in a tool failure, and tests that records are read fresh and that records_check matches aec check. Still open against her records: an independent client (item 6), per-revision behaviour beyond the echo, and a contract-version policy.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-mcp-skeleton-impl@2"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@3"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-mcp-tool-contract@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-mcp-record-reads@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/mcp.py", "sha256": "6e7112f3ea200ba4aac9930fe19a5110cffba13fd225f1ca97a0f64acc75d8f8", "locator": "q:small, standard-library MCP server over stdio", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-mcp-skeleton-impl", "version": 4, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "aec mcp serves a repository's records over the Model Context Protocol on stdio (DEC-256 item 5, first slice, an experiment under DEC-200). aec.mcp.McpServer is a standard-library JSON-RPC 2.0 server that a Telosmith-based project registers its own tools on: it answers initialize (echoing a supported revision among 2024-11-05, 2025-03-26, 2025-06-18 and 2025-11-25, else the newest), ping, tools/list and tools/call; never answers a notification; refuses batches and malformed requests with -32600, unknown methods with -32601, unknown or non-string tool names and params or arguments that are present but not objects (an omitted or null field defaults to an empty object; [], false, 0 and \"\" are refused) with -32602, and unparseable lines with -32700; checks a call's arguments against the tool's inputSchema before the handler runs (top-level required; per property type, enum and minimum; additionalProperties false when declared) and reports any problem as a result with isError, never running the handler; reports a tool's refusal as a result with isError, and an exception as a result with isError naming only the exception type (its message, which can carry paths, goes to stderr); and answers an exception in its own dispatch with -32603 for that request instead of ending the session. telosmith_server(root) adds three read-only tools over .aec/records.jsonl, read fresh on each call: records_list, record_get and records_check; every record-derived result, records_check findings and record-reading failures included, carries a notice that record text is untrusted data. Not covered: resources, prompts, HTTP transport, the A2A Agent Card, the Agent Skills folder and the authority socket (later slices). Closes gaps 1 to 3 the implementer found against Kate's AEC-R-mcp-tool-contract@1 and AEC-R-mcp-record-reads@1: argument validation, no environment details in a tool failure, and tests that records are read fresh and that records_check matches aec check. Still open against her records: an independent client (item 6), per-revision behaviour beyond the echo, and a contract-version policy. Version 4 fixes two Codex P2 findings on e4e59c3.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-mcp-skeleton-impl@3"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@3"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-mcp-tool-contract@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-mcp-record-reads@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-mcp-record-trust@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/mcp.py", "sha256": "223e9f93c2dce3c3e5ac4934c2e9671ca5d95039d6fdc952a15607f2bc3d5abd", "locator": "q:small, standard-library MCP server over stdio", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-repo-config-impl", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "aec.config reads a repository's .aec/config.json (AEC-D-repo-config@2, DEC-256 item 1, first slice). Discovery walks up from the start directory to the nearest directory holding .aec/, never past the top of the git work tree; that directory is the root and every relative path in the file resolves against it. Without the file, every setting equals today's default. With it, the whole document is validated before use: malformed JSON, a non-object top level, repeated keys, unknown top-level or nested keys, a schema version other than 1, wrong types or values, and absolute, backslash or '..' paths are each reported, all at once, in one ConfigError naming the file. Schema version 1 keys: _doc, version, records, init.ci_name, init.hook_style. Precedence is explicit flag, then the file, then the default (aec.config.resolve); aec init reads only ROOT's own config, an invalid config stops it before it writes anything, and nothing rewrites the file. aec config show prints each setting with its source; aec config check exits 0 when the file is valid or absent, else 1. Not covered yet: the records path in the commands that read records, which checks run, hook strictness and the governance options (later item-1 slices and items 3 and 4).", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@3"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-repo-config@2"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/config.py", "sha256": "189ef3ec7f811ba8b5a182b5ac359c0f26d7652e09ac0b1e04ec3db52a010ac8", "locator": "q:Per-repository configuration: `.aec/config.json`", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-repo-config-loading", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Requirement: Load `.aec/config.json` from the nearest ancestor containing `.aec/`, including but never crossing the nearest `.git` boundary; resolve configured relative paths against that selected root.", "test_must_show": ["Starting-directory, ancestor, nested-root and git-boundary cases, including `.git` as a file.", "A nearer `.aec/` without a config does not fall through to an outer config.", "An absent config supplies defaults; JSON loading works on Python 3.10.", "Configured paths resolve independently of the working directory and reject absolute paths, backslashes and `..` components."], "out_of_scope": ["TOML, config inheritance, user/global config, and symlink-based containment guarantees."], "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC--b74f392d1db5.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-20T19:19:53Z; marked [opinion] by her). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261120-23 from her proposed JSON replacements; version 2 is her numbering (her TOML round-1 versions were never committed); relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC.md round-4 ask (a behaviour summary of Telosmith#97 at 99d83b0); not the diff, test bodies, results or her round-1 records. Implementation conformance: not assessed by the maintainer.", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-repo-config@2"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-repo-config-validation", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Requirement: Validate schema version 1 strictly and report all independently detectable errors together in a diagnostic naming the config file.", "test_must_show": ["Malformed JSON, non-object roots, duplicate keys at every object level, unknown keys, and invalid types or values fail.", "`version: true` is rejected rather than accepted as integer `1`.", "`_doc` accepts only a string and has no behavioral effect.", "Multiple semantic errors appear together; unknown-key diagnostics mention that a newer Telosmith may define the key.", "Supported defaults and both hook styles validate."], "out_of_scope": ["Future schema versions, migrations and list-valued settings."], "blocking": ["Clarify “all at once”: malformed JSON need only produce its parse error; aggregation applies once parsing yields a usable structure. Do not promise exhaustive diagnostics from unparseable input."], "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC--b74f392d1db5.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-20T19:19:53Z; marked [opinion] by her). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261120-23 from her proposed JSON replacements; version 2 is her numbering (her TOML round-1 versions were never committed); relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC.md round-4 ask (a behaviour summary of Telosmith#97 at 99d83b0); not the diff, test bodies, results or her round-1 records. Implementation conformance: not assessed by the maintainer.", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-repo-config@2"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-repo-config-precedence", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Requirement: Resolve each supported setting as explicit CLI input, then file value, then default, with omitted CLI options represented distinctly from explicit values.", "test_must_show": ["Each precedence tier wins independently, including explicitly supplying a value equal to the default.", "Omitted flags do not mask configured values.", "Once record commands consume config, explicit positional `RECORDS` remains authoritative and retains its existing path interpretation."], "out_of_scope": ["Environment overrides, config merging and list replacement until lists exist."], "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC--b74f392d1db5.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-20T19:19:53Z; marked [opinion] by her). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261120-23 from her proposed JSON replacements; version 2 is her numbering (her TOML round-1 versions were never committed); relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC.md round-4 ask (a behaviour summary of Telosmith#97 at 99d83b0); not the diff, test bodies, results or her round-1 records. Implementation conformance: not assessed by the maintainer.", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-repo-config@2"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-repo-config-consumers", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Requirement: Current consumers use the validated resolver consistently, while `aec init ROOT` reads only ROOT’s own config and performs no writes if it is invalid.", "test_must_show": ["`init` ignores ancestor config, honors supported configured values and explicit overrides, and leaves the filesystem unchanged on invalid config.", "`config show` reports every supported setting’s effective value and source.", "`config check` exits zero for valid or absent config and nonzero for invalid config."], "out_of_scope": ["Record-command integration, check selection, hook strictness and governance options."], "blocking": ["Do not describe configured `records` as operational for record commands until integration and precedence tests exist; explicitly documenting it as not yet consumed is acceptable for this slice."], "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC--b74f392d1db5.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-20T19:19:53Z; marked [opinion] by her). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261120-23 from her proposed JSON replacements; version 2 is her numbering (her TOML round-1 versions were never committed); relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC.md round-4 ask (a behaviour summary of Telosmith#97 at 99d83b0); not the diff, test bodies, results or her round-1 records. Implementation conformance: not assessed by the maintainer.", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-repo-config@2"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-repo-config-impl", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "aec.config reads a repository's .aec/config.json (AEC-D-repo-config@2, DEC-256 item 1, first slice). Discovery walks up from the start directory to the nearest directory holding .aec/, never past the top of the git work tree; that directory is the root and every relative path in the file resolves against it. Without the file, every setting equals today's default. With it, the whole document is validated before use: malformed JSON, a non-object top level, repeated keys, unknown top-level or nested keys, a schema version other than 1, wrong types or values, and absolute, backslash or '..' paths are each reported, all at once, in one ConfigError naming the file. Schema version 1 keys: _doc, version, records, init.ci_name, init.hook_style. Precedence is explicit flag, then the file, then the default (aec.config.resolve); aec init reads only ROOT's own config, an invalid config stops it before it writes anything, and nothing rewrites the file. aec config show prints each setting with its source; aec config check exits 0 when the file is valid or absent, else 1. Second slice: the commands whose records path is optional read the records key. aec source show|search, aec import-purpose and aec mcp use, in order, an explicit --records path (unchanged meaning, relative to the working directory; the config is then not read), records in ROOT's own .aec/config.json resolved against ROOT (never a parent's), else ROOT/.aec/records.jsonl as before (aec.config.records_path). aec speckit derive|drift, which already search upward, use records from the config found by discovery from the feature, else the nearest .aec/records.jsonl as before (aec.config.discovered_records). An invalid config is an error only where it would be used. A required positional RECORDS (aec check, impact, code-impact, append) is unchanged and never becomes optional. Not covered yet: the editor hook (aec hook), which checks run, hook strictness and the governance options (items 2 to 4).", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@3"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-repo-config@2"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/config.py", "sha256": "53960179762c8dd063c9ae55ede68df1d3a4ec00aa67731ceb8f504e684b54c2", "locator": "q:Per-repository configuration: `.aec/config.json`", "for": "text"}, {"path": "src/aec/config.py", "sha256": "53960179762c8dd063c9ae55ede68df1d3a4ec00aa67731ceb8f504e684b54c2", "locator": "q:def records_path", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-repo-config-records", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "text": "Requirement: Records consumers must select explicit `--records` relative to cwd without reading config, otherwise use the applicable config’s `records` relative to its repository root, otherwise use the command’s default records path, preserving explicit-ROOT isolation, speckit discovery, positional RECORDS behavior, and hook independence.", "test_must_show": ["Each ROOT-taking consumer selects explicit → ROOT-local config → `ROOT/.aec/records.jsonl`. Cover `source show`, `source search`, `import-purpose`, and `mcp`. Run from a different cwd; give parent and ROOT conflicting configs. A parent config is never used.", "Each speckit consumer selects explicit → discovered config → nearest default records file. Cover both `derive` and `drift`, with competing ancestor fixtures.", "Explicit relative paths resolve against cwd; configured relative paths resolve against the selected repository root.", "Missing config, and valid config without `records`, preserve fallback behavior.", "Invalid config errors when consulted, but not when explicit records bypass it.", "Required positional RECORDS commands and the editor hook remain unaffected by config’s `records`, including invalid values."], "out_of_scope": ["Other config fields, changing discovery boundaries, record-content validation, automatic file creation, and migration of repositories."], "blocking": ["Specification blocker: pin down speckit’s discovery interaction. State whether a discovered config without `records` causes immediate fallback to the nearest records file or continued config discovery. Define what stops discovery and which root anchors the selected config’s relative path. Existing discovery rules can satisfy this by explicit reference; they need not be redesigned."], "source": "kate-replies:replies/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC--d2c6854b70f2.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-21T01:19:41Z; marked [opinion] by her). Transcribed verbatim by claude:aec#wake-20261121-05; her bullets under 'Tests must show' are joined one item per top-level bullet. She proposed it as a revision of `AEC-R-repo-config-impl@2`; that id and version already hold the implementer's own record, so the transcriber filed it under this new id rather than mix authorship in one id's versions. Relations added by the transcriber.", "shown": "relay-kit-private handoffs/outputs/HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC.md round-5 ask (a behaviour summary of Telosmith#98 at f50e5dc); not the diff, record bodies, discovery implementation or test results. Implementation conformance: not assessed by the maintainer.", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-repo-config@2"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-repo-config-precedence@2"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-repo-config-impl", "version": 3, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "aec.config reads a repository's .aec/config.json (AEC-D-repo-config@2, DEC-256 item 1, first slice). Discovery walks up from the start directory to the nearest directory holding .aec/, never past the top of the git work tree; that directory is the root and every relative path in the file resolves against it. Without the file, every setting equals today's default. With it, the whole document is validated before use: malformed JSON, a non-object top level, repeated keys, unknown top-level or nested keys, a schema version other than 1, wrong types or values, and absolute, backslash or '..' paths are each reported, all at once, in one ConfigError naming the file. Schema version 1 keys: _doc, version, records, init.ci_name, init.hook_style. Precedence is explicit flag, then the file, then the default (aec.config.resolve); aec init reads only ROOT's own config, an invalid config stops it before it writes anything, and nothing rewrites the file. aec config show prints each setting with its source; aec config check exits 0 when the file is valid or absent, else 1. Second slice: the commands whose records path is optional read the records key. aec source show|search, aec import-purpose and aec mcp use, in order, an explicit --records path (unchanged meaning, relative to the working directory; the config is then not read), records in ROOT's own .aec/config.json resolved against ROOT (never a parent's), else ROOT/.aec/records.jsonl as before (aec.config.records_path). aec speckit derive|drift, which already search upward, use records from the config found by discovery from the feature, else the nearest .aec/records.jsonl as before (aec.config.discovered_records). An invalid config is an error only where it would be used. A configured records path is refused (ConfigError) when any component below the root is a symlink or when it resolves outside the root, so a committed link can't send a read or an append outside the repository (aec.config.configured_records; Codex security review on #98). A required positional RECORDS (aec check, impact, code-impact, append) is unchanged and never becomes optional. Not covered yet: the editor hook (aec hook), which checks run, hook strictness and the governance options (items 2 to 4).", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@3"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-repo-config@2"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/config.py", "sha256": "252ce5589e621186d6d20c55c5d22997c7228f173ce72bc60ef1b4b9c14422b5", "locator": "q:Per-repository configuration: `.aec/config.json`", "for": "text"}, {"path": "src/aec/config.py", "sha256": "252ce5589e621186d6d20c55c5d22997c7228f173ce72bc60ef1b4b9c14422b5", "locator": "q:def configured_records", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-hook-line", "version": 5, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "aec init --hook-style line writes a project hook whose settings text holds only the launcher and a pre-import gate, which calls aec hook project, the hook body shipped in the package. Before any aec code runs, the gate (one python3 -I -B process started from /; outside a virtual environment and unless PYTHONNOUSERSITE is set, the user site is put back ahead of the system site-packages as a plain path, so its .pth files and usercustomize never run; the filtered PYTHONPATH entries are appended after the interpreter's own path) requires commit in tools/aec_upstream.json to be a full 40-character SHA in a regular file, finds aec without importing it, and accepts it only when it belongs to an installed telosmith distribution whose PEP 610 metadata is a non-editable git install of exactly that commit, outside the project; it then loads that same spec and runs the body in the same process. A missing or malformed pin, no importable aec, a source checkout, an editable install, another commit or version-control system, a shadowing aec earlier on the path, or a pinned aec without hook project each exits 1 with one line saying which; for an install that is not the pinned git commit the line names the pinned and the installed commit and the pip command. On the same checkout with a pinned install it exits as the inline hook does: 0 when quiet, 1 when a step could not run, 2 with a report for the agent; a symlink at .aec, the records file or either output is refused. inline stays the default. Out of scope: tampering with the installed environment (the user-level hook verifies RECORD), aec init writing the pin file, and replacing any repository's existing hook.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AEC-R-hook-line@4"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-hook-launcher-preimport@2"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-hook-line-pin-gate@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-pin-check-local-identity@2"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-pin-check-scope@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-braided-dcc@1"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:src.aec.userhook.project_run"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-R-hook-safe-path@6"}], "source": "Implementer-written. @4 plus the user site (Codex P2 on eraevous/MtG#59: -I hid pip install --user installs) and the installed commit in the mismatch line (Kate, DBN5 round 14, kate-replies HO-AEC-20261117-DBN5--828b4560e6cb). Tests: tests/test_project_hook_line.py PreImportGate.", "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/init.py", "sha256": "18614c5af3ce9056205606170129f935588845b6a664a426c3438bb6f88b2096", "locator": "q:HOOK_LINE_GATE = (", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "AEC-R-snippets-render-impl", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:aec", "author_role": "implementer", "text": "aec snippets renders the hook and CI snippets aec init writes, from the repository's own config, so repositories need not commit .aec/snippets/ (DEC-256 item 3, HO-AEC-20261119-V8FC). `aec snippets show hook` prints the settings JSON for init.hook_style (default inline); `aec snippets show ci` prints the CI workflow for init.ci_name (default aec) pinned to --ref (a full 40-character SHA only) or else the commit in tools/aec_upstream.json; it never resolves a commit over the network and exits 1 naming what to supply when neither exists, and never reads the pin through a symlinked tools/ directory. Only ROOT's own .aec/config.json counts; an invalid config fails. For the same settings and commit, show prints byte for byte what aec init writes, for both hook styles. `aec snippets check` compares each file under .aec/snippets/: claude-settings.json as JSON, <name>-ci.yml as text; a CI file named for another ci_name, a CI file with no commit to compare against, a symlink or non-regular file each count as a problem; other files are listed, not failed; exit 0 only when there are no problems; it writes nothing. New config key init.snippet_files (bool, default true, so aec init is unchanged): false makes aec init write no snippet copies and point its next steps to `aec snippets show hook` and `aec snippets show ci --ref <commit>`. Out of scope: removing committed copies from other repositories (follow-up PRs), writing .claude/settings.json or workflow files, and flipping the default.", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "AEC-P0@3"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AEC-D-repo-config@2"}], "anchors": [{"path": "src/aec/snippets.py", "sha256": "43905af121660afa33c99986c515a0b0bbc00b841d736169e80b96b62b57b7b8", "locator": "q:render the hook and CI snippets from the repository", "for": "text"}]}
